WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.569
- It's also millions
and millions of people.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:06.573 align:start size:84% position:16%
Not only millions
of people in Israel,

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
millions of Jews
throughout the world,

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.946
but millions of non-Jews who
see in the story of Israel

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.983
a parable for humanity.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:19.019
Because if the Jewish people

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
can overcome the most
dreadful odds in history,

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.124
can come back from the dead,

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:29.129
can ford this river between
annihilation and salvation

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.500
and build this remarkable state,

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
then there's hope
for all of humanity.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.038
(calm music)

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.644
- I am Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.547 align:start size:84% position:16%
is the twice and
future prime minister

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.815
of the state of Israel

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:52.552
and author of the new
book, "Bibi: My Story".

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:84% position:16%
Prime Minister
Benjamin Netanyahu,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.256
Welcome to "The Rubin Report".

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.757
- Good to be with you. Pleased.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.559
- You know, I have to say,

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've watched you
obviously on television,

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:84% position:16%
a million interviews
over the years,

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.765
speaking at the UN,
all kinds of things,

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.834
and one of the things
that I always think

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.603
when you are speaking or
any advocate for Israel,

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.505
is why don't they
show more maps?

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:16.142
Just show a map of the Middle
East and the size of Israel

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.878
verse, you know, the entire
region and everything else.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.947
And then I get a
copy of your book,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.450
and we're gonna show you
the full thing on screen,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.984
but I'm gonna hold it
up for just a moment.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's exactly how the
book begins, right?

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.923
The opening flap right there,

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.459
just to give a little
context to the size.

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:33.793 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I thought that would
be an interesting way

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.662
to start the conversation.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.030
- Wait a minute, wait a minute.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to do something.
Open that book.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.333 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yes.
- Put your thumb,

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.668
put your finger on Israel

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:44.337
so they get a feeling
for the Arab world.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:45.572
This is Israel, right?

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.373
- Yes, exactly.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:51.044 align:start position:0%
- And don't even begin to
encompass the Arab world or Iran

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:56.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
in these two flaps, so
that's my two cents' worth

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.984
of the proportion.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.552
- Yeah, well, I thought it
was a nice way to start,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.954
because basically
when people look

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.655
at most maps of the world,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.591
you can't even fit one letter

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.494
of the word Israel
on Israel itself.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.497 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I feel like if
people understood that
a little bit more,

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:13.233
maybe they'd be perhaps
a little bit kinder,

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.769
is that just naivete as someone
that's been defending Israel

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.105
for 60 plus years?

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.574
- Well, it's wishful
thinking, but yeah.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.576
I guess when people are
exposed to the facts,

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.613
which many are not, yeah,
they see it differently,

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they realize that
Israel is a tiny country,

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.951
but it's a gigantic country.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:36.022 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because even though we
constitute less than one 10th,

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.825
one 10th of 1% of the
world's population,

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.460
we have been consistently ranked

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:45.465
in the decade that I led the
country between 2010 and 2020

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:97% position:3%
as the eighth most powerful
country in the world,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:56.309
which is kind of unbelievable,
I mean, when you think of it.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.079 align:start size:81% position:19%
And that is, I
suppose, not only,

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.581
you can explain that rationally,

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:04.751
but I think it's a miracle
of faith and resolution.

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.320 align:start size:81% position:19%
Israel, because
of the resolution,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:12.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
the resolve of its citizens,
the genius of its people

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:17.730 align:start position:0%
has become the juggernaut
innovation nation in the world.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.267
We've just crossed in GDP,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:25.405 align:start size:84% position:16%
we've crossed Japan,
France, Britain,

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.075
and Germany, GDP per capita.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:31.711 align:start size:88% position:13%
And remember, I describe
this in my book,

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:35.081
when we began the
economic revolution

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.584
towards free markets,
away from socialism,

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:40.420
we were basically the last
place in Western Europe,

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.989
and now we're pretty
much in first place,

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.391
and we're gonna catch up
with the United States.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.461
That's a personal quest.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.896
I'm not saying that we'll
beat the United States,

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:52.432 align:start size:88% position:13%
but we'll catch up
with the United States.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.567 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So as I described
in the opening,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.503 align:start size:97% position:3%
you are the twice and future
prime minister of Israel.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
As we speak right now,
you're in the midst

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.274
of forming this coalition.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.675
You have the mandate to do it.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.877
You've done this a
couple times before,

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.713
but Israel seems to
have elections every,

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.881
what, six months or so.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.116
Are you confident

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.351
that you're gonna pull
this thing together?

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:13.219
I mean, this one looks
a little more solid,

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.788
I guess, than the
last few, right?

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.390
- Yeah, well we had...

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.891
First of all, this
is the sixth time

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.727
I'm forming a government.

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:24.163 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I've been Israel's longest
serving prime minister,

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:27.400 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I describe my
travails and triumphs

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the course of that
very long career.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:34.007 align:start size:97% position:3%
Within a year, I'll be the
longest serving elected leader

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:37.210
of a democracy in
over half a century

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.811
of any place in the world.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.913
But somebody put me
a note the other day,

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.415 align:start size:84% position:16%
gave me a note,
and he said, "Well,

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.617 align:start size:84% position:16%
you should know that
there are leaders

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.586 align:start size:84% position:16%
who've come back from
political death."

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.021
Churchill, one example.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:52.225 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yitzhak Rabin in
Israel is another one.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.627 align:start size:84% position:16%
But this fellow told
me, "I've checked

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.329 align:start size:84% position:16%
when was the last time
somebody came back

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.231
from political death twice?"

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:01.200 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he said, "That happened
3/4 of a century ago."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.071
So I don't belittle
the task before me,

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:10.043 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I think after a succession
of indecisive elections

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:12.145
in the formation of
a peculiar government

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:15.081
that was brought
down after a year,

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:18.251 align:start size:97% position:3%
we now have a solid
majority, a coherent majority

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:21.821
to form a center right
and right government,

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.523
coherent in policy

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:26.626
that will, I think, take
Israel and the Middle East

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:31.564
to fantastic places, contrary
to the left-leaning press.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.833
Will get more peace treaties,

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:37.970 align:start size:97% position:3%
perhaps end the Arab-Israeli
conflict altogether.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.006 align:start size:97% position:3%
Not the Palestinian-Israeli
conflict,

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:41.574
the conflict with
the Arab world,

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:45.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is 99 times the
size of the Palestinians.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:49.415
And block Iran, and
develop technologies

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:53.586
that will stupefy the world
and service all of humanity.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.023
These are some of the
goals that I have,

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.825 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I think they're
within reach.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.560 align:start size:81% position:19%
Yes, I think it'll
be more stable

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.195
and I think it'll be successful.

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:05.064
- You mention a center
right or right coalition.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.567
Can you sort of compare
how that's different

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.169
than, say, an American right?

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.572
I know you're a student of
American politics as well,

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:15.074 align:start position:0%
but for you guys, the right
is, it's a little bit different

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:18.277
just by the nature
of the demographics
and everything else.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:20.880 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Well, I think
the, first of all,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.148
it's a parliamentary system.

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.983
So you have to cobble
together a coalition.

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.152 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's not as if the prime
minister is elected

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:28.521 align:start size:81% position:19%
by popular vote
like the president

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:31.157
and he can choose his
cabinet and so on.

00:06:31.157 --> 00:06:32.558
This is not the way--
- Do you get jealous

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:34.260
of our two party system
when you're in the midst

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.729
of trying to cobble
this thing together?

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.531
- Wildly so.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:41.100 align:start size:81% position:19%
Envious to the
roots of my being.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:45.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because cobbling together
a coalition is like,

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.740 align:start size:84% position:16%
you're familiar
with a Rubik's Cube,

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.575 align:start size:81% position:19%
you know?
- Yeah, of course.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.277
- Turn one and then

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:53.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to turn the
other one and it matches,

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.647 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you turn, and
you think you got it,

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:55.915 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then the last
piece doesn't match,

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.517
you have to start
all over again?

00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:58.818
That's more or less
what I've been doing

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.119
over the last few weeks,

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.121
but I think I'm getting there.

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:05.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is not Rubin's Cube,
this is Rubik's Cube.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.560
(Dave laughs)
And I'm Rubik.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.963 align:start position:0%
So at the end, I have to be
Rubik or there's no government.

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:13.099
There will be a government.

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:15.034
So the first thing is

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:17.770
you have to cobble
together a coalition,

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:21.340
that is a majority in the
members of the parliament

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.742
or congress, if you will,

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:24.277 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they choose
the prime minister.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:27.814
And obviously if we put it
together, they'll choose me.

00:07:27.814 --> 00:07:29.816
That's the first change.

00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:32.819
The second change is you have
a multiplicity of parties.

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:34.320
You don't have two parties,

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have, I don't know,
12 parties in the Knesset,

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.757
something like that.

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:39.992
And the third thing is that

00:07:41.727 --> 00:07:45.398
the right in Israel is
first of all premised,

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.934 align:start size:84% position:16%
the differences
between left and right

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:51.437
are premised first of all in
the intensity that you put

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.005
on the question of security.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:56.442
Security is the number one
issue in Israeli elections.

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:58.211
The economy is a second.

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.314
Sometimes a distance second.

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:08.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say the intensity
of identification

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:12.558
with the Jewish state
and how you protect it

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:15.895
is really what guides
Israeli elections,

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:17.964 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that's what brought
me to office here,

00:08:17.964 --> 00:08:20.233
because the outgoing government,

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:22.468
to cobble together
their coalition,

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:28.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
basically made a pact with
a party, an Arab party,

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:33.279
that identifies with
the Muslim Brotherhood.

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:38.284 align:start position:0%
The Muslim brotherhood who
won't recognize the Jewish state

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:40.786 align:start size:84% position:16%
and wants to dissolve
the Jewish state.

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.154
Now obviously the
outgoing coalition

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.123 align:start size:84% position:16%
didn't wanna dissolve
the Jewish state,

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:47.894 align:start size:97% position:3%
but they made themselves
hostage to a party that does

00:08:47.894 --> 00:08:48.828
in order to stay in power.

00:08:48.828 --> 00:08:51.097
Well, that didn't last long

00:08:51.097 --> 00:08:53.966 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it was brought down,
and now I assure you,

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:55.635
that's not gonna be repeated.

00:08:55.635 --> 00:08:58.004
By the way, many
Arabs support me.

00:08:58.004 --> 00:08:59.972
Many Arabs vote for the Likud.

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:02.041
Arabs have served in the Likud,

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:05.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
and can serve in any
government in the future.

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:10.416
But the issue is not the
ethnicity of the voters,

00:09:11.617 --> 00:09:12.785
or the ministers, or
the Knesset members,

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:14.320
it's their ideology.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.055
And once the ideology,

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:18.691
to which unfortunately
some Jews subscribe, too,

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:20.059
Jewish Knesset members,

00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:23.963 align:start position:0%
that Israel should be dissolved,
destroyed, eliminated,

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:26.399 align:start size:88% position:13%
obviously that didn't
do well with the voters,

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:31.404
so here we are, we have
a way to correct this.

00:09:31.404 --> 00:09:33.940
- How do you balance
some of the tensions

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:37.343
between the secular people
and the more religious people

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:39.812
as someone that's gonna be
prime minister for everybody?

00:09:39.812 --> 00:09:42.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've obviously done this
a couple times before,

00:09:42.648 --> 00:09:44.317
obviously very successfully.

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:47.553
But that that's one of
the sort of fissures

00:09:47.553 --> 00:09:49.021
in Israeli society.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:53.092 align:start size:97% position:3%
- What you do in any
democracy is you compromise.

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:54.527
You make compromises.

00:09:54.527 --> 00:09:56.429
There are things you
don't compromise about.

00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:59.665 align:start size:97% position:3%
On Israel's existence, on
security, I don't compromise.

00:09:59.665 --> 00:10:00.900
And if I have to stand up

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.602
and go to a joint
session of Congress

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:08.240 align:start size:97% position:3%
to challenge a person I
respected, but disagreed with,

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.245
President Obama, he wanted to
pass this, and did actually,

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:18.017 align:start size:81% position:19%
this dangerous
Iran nuclear deal,

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:21.520
which would pave Iran's path
with gold to a nuclear arsenal.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.955
Well, I thought,
I have no choice,

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:25.491 align:start size:97% position:3%
I have to go and take a stand
and gave a speech there,

00:10:25.491 --> 00:10:27.426
which I describe in detail.

00:10:28.694 --> 00:10:31.130
So there are things you
don't compromise about.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:34.100 align:start size:84% position:16%
But in political
life in democracies,

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.901
that's what you constantly do.

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:40.239 align:start size:97% position:3%
You either come to an
agreement with opposing views,

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:41.607 align:start size:84% position:16%
and if you don't
come to an agreement,

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:44.510
you bring it to a vote.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:49.215 align:start size:81% position:19%
And often you come
to an agreement

00:10:49.215 --> 00:10:52.418 align:start position:0%
by arriving at some kind of
balance between opposing views,

00:10:52.418 --> 00:10:53.686
and that's being done every day.

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:55.321
You do it in the
American Congress,

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:56.956
you do it in the
Israeli Knesset.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.925
- So as someone that's,

00:10:59.925 --> 00:11:02.228 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're basically the
same age as the country,

00:11:02.228 --> 00:11:06.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
within a couple years, and
you were born in a time

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:08.234 align:start size:88% position:13%
when the country was
trying to come together,

00:11:08.234 --> 00:11:09.402
was obviously not powerful,

00:11:09.402 --> 00:11:11.270
it was a couple miracles

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.240 align:start size:97% position:3%
basically to even come
into existence as a nation,

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.642 align:start size:88% position:13%
versus now where
there's a military might

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:19.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
and an economic power
that you're talking about.

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:21.547
How different is that
for the Israeli psyche,

00:11:21.547 --> 00:11:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
or even just for you as
the leader of the country,

00:11:23.983 --> 00:11:27.319 align:start size:88% position:13%
knowing what the
country was 50 years ago

00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:30.222
compared to where
it's at in 2022?

00:11:30.222 --> 00:11:35.227 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I described
the roots of my views,

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:37.797 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it's very much
influenced by my father,

00:11:37.797 --> 00:11:39.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was a great historian
of the Jewish people.

00:11:39.665 --> 00:11:42.101
But what he taught me was that

00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:46.172
there is no finality
in the life of nations.

00:11:46.172 --> 00:11:47.840
Nations have come and
nations have gone,

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:50.676
and the Jewish people are
perhaps unique in the fact

00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:54.547 align:start size:97% position:3%
that having lost our country,
having lost our state,

00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:57.416 align:start size:97% position:3%
having been dispersed to the
far corners of the earth,

00:11:57.416 --> 00:12:01.554 align:start position:0%
we actually came back and
reconstituted our national life

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:05.291
in our home, in our tiny
homeland, but our homeland.

00:12:05.291 --> 00:12:07.927
And the fact that
we did that was,

00:12:07.927 --> 00:12:11.964
I would say the mission of
restoring Jewish nationhood

00:12:11.964 --> 00:12:15.634
and Jewish independence
in the land of Israel

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:18.871 align:start size:88% position:13%
was the task that
informed my grandfather

00:12:20.306 --> 00:12:24.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
and my father in founding
and helping found the state.

00:12:24.443 --> 00:12:29.448
The task that I inherited
was to secure the future,

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:34.153
the prosperity and especially
the security and permanence

00:12:34.153 --> 00:12:37.123
of this state, because
it's not guaranteed.

00:12:37.123 --> 00:12:39.592
Well, what guarantees,

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:46.065
the life of states
in a turbulent world,

00:12:46.065 --> 00:12:47.666
which is often cruel?

00:12:47.666 --> 00:12:51.637 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, for some
people on the left,

00:12:51.637 --> 00:12:53.839
they think that if you're moral

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:58.811 align:start size:88% position:13%
and if you put up a nice
facade to the world,

00:13:00.246 --> 00:13:03.415
a compliant facade, then
history will protect you.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.787 align:start size:88% position:13%
In fact, they often
quote Martin Luther King

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:12.792 align:start position:0%
who said that "The arc of
history bends towards justice."

00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:17.396
Maybe so, but it is
a very brittle arc

00:13:17.396 --> 00:13:22.001
and it could break under the
pounding of the darkest forces,

00:13:22.001 --> 00:13:26.405 align:start position:0%
the totalitarian and dictatorial
and ideological forces

00:13:26.405 --> 00:13:29.275
that are opposed to the very
idea of freedom and justice.

00:13:30.676 --> 00:13:35.147 align:start size:97% position:3%
And history doesn't favor
morality, it favors strength.

00:13:35.881 --> 00:13:37.149
That's what it does.

00:13:37.149 --> 00:13:38.818
That's why Genghis Khan
could conquer the world

00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:44.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
and hold on, that empire
could hold on for a century.

00:13:44.423 --> 00:13:46.692 align:start size:88% position:13%
Through enormous
subjugation, the Romans,

00:13:46.692 --> 00:13:47.960
whatever you think of them,

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.162
held it for many,
many more centuries

00:13:50.162 --> 00:13:53.532
through just sheer power,
sheer cohesion and power.

00:13:53.532 --> 00:13:56.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
And does it guarantee that
our free civilization,

00:13:56.268 --> 00:13:59.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
does history guarantee
that our free civilization

00:13:59.205 --> 00:14:01.574 align:start size:84% position:16%
will triumph over
totalitarian forces?

00:14:01.574 --> 00:14:04.276
And the answer is
categorically not.

00:14:04.276 --> 00:14:07.613
If they can amass
greater economic,

00:14:07.613 --> 00:14:10.182
military, and political power,

00:14:10.182 --> 00:14:12.518
especially economic
and military power,

00:14:12.518 --> 00:14:13.752
then they'll overcome you

00:14:13.752 --> 00:14:16.188 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you don't have enough
countervailing force.

00:14:16.188 --> 00:14:18.257
Israel, being a tiny country,

00:14:18.257 --> 00:14:20.926 align:start size:84% position:16%
had to be enormously
more powerful

00:14:20.926 --> 00:14:22.528
given that it was
surrounded at first

00:14:22.528 --> 00:14:25.464 align:start position:0%
by hundreds of millions of
Arabs who wanted to destroy it,

00:14:26.632 --> 00:14:30.069 align:start size:88% position:13%
and lately by about a
hundred million Iranians

00:14:30.069 --> 00:14:31.570
who don't want to destroy it,

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:34.273
but are governed by these
theological thugs who do

00:14:34.273 --> 00:14:36.308
and openly declare
death to Israel,

00:14:36.308 --> 00:14:38.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
and by the way,
death to America too,

00:14:38.143 --> 00:14:39.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
but they're building
atomic bombs,

00:14:39.712 --> 00:14:42.014
or that's what they seek
to do, to destroy Israel.

00:14:42.014 --> 00:14:44.917
So you need to be
very, very strong.

00:14:44.917 --> 00:14:47.686
I devoted my life, as
I describe in my book,

00:14:47.686 --> 00:14:50.623
to empower Israel,

00:14:51.824 --> 00:14:53.259
not to subjugate others,

00:14:53.259 --> 00:14:55.461
but to defend itself from others

00:14:55.461 --> 00:14:58.697
and to make sure that
nobody could destroy

00:14:58.697 --> 00:15:01.300 align:start size:97% position:3%
the one and only Jewish state
once it was reconstituted

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:03.269
after thousands of years.

00:15:03.269 --> 00:15:05.104
The one thing that,

00:15:05.104 --> 00:15:06.672
and all Israelis
understood that.

00:15:06.672 --> 00:15:09.008 align:start size:97% position:3%
They understood that we
have to have a strong army.

00:15:09.008 --> 00:15:12.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
The first prime minister,
David Ben-Gurion,

00:15:12.011 --> 00:15:15.114 align:start size:97% position:3%
invested an enormous effort
to build such an army.

00:15:15.114 --> 00:15:18.317
But I came to the conclusion
that it couldn't be sustained.

00:15:19.685 --> 00:15:23.989 align:start size:97% position:3%
It couldn't be sustained
because F-35 fighter aircraft,

00:15:23.989 --> 00:15:28.994
submarines, drones, cyber
intelligence and so on,

00:15:29.862 --> 00:15:31.163
they have one common quality:

00:15:31.163 --> 00:15:34.166
They cost money, a lot of money.

00:15:34.166 --> 00:15:36.535
And if you have a
socialist economy,

00:15:36.535 --> 00:15:39.038 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're not gonna be
able to pay for defense.

00:15:39.038 --> 00:15:41.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
Typically the way
Israelis thought about it,

00:15:41.106 --> 00:15:42.641
well, the government
will produce the money.

00:15:42.641 --> 00:15:44.910
How will they produce the
money? Well, tax the rich.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.512 align:start size:84% position:16%
Tax the rich,
well, first of all,

00:15:46.512 --> 00:15:49.248 align:start size:97% position:3%
there are not enough rich
people in a socialist economy.

00:15:49.248 --> 00:15:52.484
And secondly, those who are
will move to other places

00:15:52.484 --> 00:15:54.019
when you overtax them.

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:58.524
I came with a radical idea,
which I describe in my book,

00:15:58.524 --> 00:16:03.295
that there's a thing called
free markets capitalism.

00:16:03.295 --> 00:16:05.164
And that's the way we generate

00:16:05.164 --> 00:16:09.034
both a better life for our
people, a higher income,

00:16:09.034 --> 00:16:10.602
a higher distribution of income

00:16:10.602 --> 00:16:15.607
compared to what the socialist
leaning people were thinking,

00:16:17.209 --> 00:16:20.612
but also it gives us
the wherewithal to
fund our military.

00:16:20.612 --> 00:16:22.348
And therefore, I initiated

00:16:23.449 --> 00:16:25.584 align:start size:84% position:16%
a free market
revolution in Israel

00:16:25.584 --> 00:16:28.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
that made Israel
into this juggernaut,

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:32.624
this free market juggernaut
of the innovation nation

00:16:34.026 --> 00:16:35.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
that can compete with
any country in the world,

00:16:35.661 --> 00:16:39.131
and in fact does, and
that changed Israel.

00:16:39.131 --> 00:16:41.400
It gave it the economic power

00:16:42.868 --> 00:16:44.703
to have military power,

00:16:44.703 --> 00:16:47.439
and the combination of the
two gave us diplomatic power,

00:16:47.439 --> 00:16:50.509
and that is what can
guarantee our future.

00:16:50.509 --> 00:16:52.044
Not forever.

00:16:52.044 --> 00:16:54.413
I don't know of anything
that protects you forever.

00:16:54.413 --> 00:16:55.981
But for the coming decades,

00:16:55.981 --> 00:16:58.717 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that's what I intend
to nurture further

00:16:58.717 --> 00:17:03.155 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the coming years in my
next tenure as prime minister.

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:05.524
- So I wanna get back
to the economic stuff

00:17:05.524 --> 00:17:07.659 align:start position:0%
because I think it's super
interesting that you guys went,

00:17:07.659 --> 00:17:11.363
in essence, from a socialist
nation to a capitalist nation,

00:17:11.363 --> 00:17:12.598
and then in economic prowess.

00:17:12.598 --> 00:17:13.999
Where in the United States

00:17:13.999 --> 00:17:16.702 align:start position:0%
we seem to be doing some
version of the reverse of that,

00:17:16.702 --> 00:17:18.904 align:start size:97% position:3%
at least at the moment,
hopefully not for too long.

00:17:18.904 --> 00:17:21.140
But on some of the security
stuff you just mentioned,

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.342
you were sort of way ahead

00:17:23.342 --> 00:17:25.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
when it came to
the Gaza withdrawal

00:17:25.411 --> 00:17:26.979
of 20 some odd years ago.

00:17:26.979 --> 00:17:29.181
You were not for it
when Sharon did it,

00:17:29.181 --> 00:17:30.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you said it would
not bring peace.

00:17:30.949 --> 00:17:32.918
Clearly that was proven correct.

00:17:32.918 --> 00:17:35.020
When you talk to your
lefty counterparts,

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:37.623 align:start size:84% position:16%
or if they're willing
to talk to you,

00:17:37.623 --> 00:17:39.158
do they still believe that, oh,

00:17:39.158 --> 00:17:41.593
if we just give away enough land

00:17:41.593 --> 00:17:43.996
that actually that
would provide peace?

00:17:43.996 --> 00:17:46.498
I mean, are there really
thought leaders on the left

00:17:46.498 --> 00:17:49.201
that believe those
things at this point?

00:17:49.201 --> 00:17:51.437
Or is it just posturing?

00:17:51.437 --> 00:17:53.138 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, no, I think
some of them believe it,

00:17:53.138 --> 00:17:55.207
but they also avoid
talking about it

00:17:56.575 --> 00:17:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
because most of the
public doesn't accept it.

00:17:58.811 --> 00:18:00.712
Why? Because we tried it.

00:18:00.712 --> 00:18:02.948
So we left, we vacated Lebanon.

00:18:02.948 --> 00:18:05.617
The argument was you give
territory, you get peace.

00:18:05.617 --> 00:18:06.552
Territory for peace.

00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:08.887
Okay, we left Lebanon

00:18:08.887 --> 00:18:10.355 align:start size:81% position:19%
and that territory
was taken over

00:18:10.355 --> 00:18:13.459
by proxies of Iran, Hezbollah,

00:18:13.459 --> 00:18:17.029
who fired 10,000 rockets
since then into Israel.

00:18:17.029 --> 00:18:18.197
We left Gaza,

00:18:19.398 --> 00:18:21.867
again with the hope that
this would create peace,

00:18:21.867 --> 00:18:24.970
and this was taken over
by another proxy of Iran,

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.941
or a close ally of Iran, Hamas,

00:18:28.941 --> 00:18:31.677
and they fired 10,000
rockets into Israel.

00:18:31.677 --> 00:18:35.047
And if you say, all right, so
let's leave Judea, Samaria,

00:18:35.047 --> 00:18:39.985
which is the heartland, the
biblical heartland of Israel

00:18:39.985 --> 00:18:43.122
and envelopes Jerusalem

00:18:43.122 --> 00:18:47.993 align:start position:0%
and is within spitting distance
of Tel Aviv, just leave.

00:18:47.993 --> 00:18:50.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Israel, by the way,
would become 10 miles wide

00:18:50.762 --> 00:18:51.597
with its back.

00:18:53.065 --> 00:18:54.867 align:start size:88% position:13%
And just shut your
eyes, hope for the best,

00:18:54.867 --> 00:18:57.336
and hope that what happened
in Lebanon with Hezbollah,

00:18:57.336 --> 00:19:00.506
what happened in Gaza with Hamas

00:19:00.506 --> 00:19:03.976 align:start size:97% position:3%
doesn't recur in Judea,
Samara, the West Bank, okay?

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
People can't buy that now,
because we've tried it.

00:19:07.646 --> 00:19:09.948
You know, fool me
once, shame on me.

00:19:09.948 --> 00:19:11.416
Fool me twice, you know that.

00:19:13.051 --> 00:19:14.353
People are not gonna do that.

00:19:14.353 --> 00:19:16.922
So you ask, do they believe it?

00:19:16.922 --> 00:19:19.158
They probably cling
to it as a religious,

00:19:20.325 --> 00:19:23.962
sort of a religious,
quasi-religious belief

00:19:23.962 --> 00:19:25.531 align:start size:88% position:13%
that they don't
(indistinct) right away,

00:19:25.531 --> 00:19:28.600
but politically, this
simply didn't come up

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.503
in the previous elections,
it just wasn't an issue.

00:19:31.503 --> 00:19:32.771
Not at all.

00:19:32.771 --> 00:19:37.242
And you know, the issue
was me. I was the issue.

00:19:37.242 --> 00:19:41.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
They basically said, the issue
wasn't Israel's security,

00:19:43.215 --> 00:19:45.884 align:start size:88% position:13%
not the idea of creating
a Palestinian state,

00:19:45.884 --> 00:19:48.921 align:start size:88% position:13%
which would be an
armed Palestinian state

00:19:48.921 --> 00:19:50.689
committed to our destruction.

00:19:50.689 --> 00:19:52.191
People didn't buy that.

00:19:52.191 --> 00:19:54.760
- Right, it would also be
two states, wouldn't it?

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:56.361
Wouldn't, in essence,
there would be two.

00:19:56.361 --> 00:19:58.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it would really
be a three-state solution,

00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.831
not a two-state solution,

00:19:59.831 --> 00:20:02.701
because Gaza and the West Bank
obviously are not connected.

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:04.269
People don't seem to
really understand that.

00:20:04.269 --> 00:20:05.938
- Gaza's already
been thrown away,

00:20:05.938 --> 00:20:08.574
and it's effectively
an independent state

00:20:08.574 --> 00:20:10.409
surrounded by Israel and Egypt,

00:20:10.409 --> 00:20:12.044
but it's an independent state.

00:20:12.044 --> 00:20:13.512
Well, what do they do with it?

00:20:13.512 --> 00:20:15.914 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, they build
tunnels, terror tunnels,

00:20:15.914 --> 00:20:18.116
in order to penetrate
us, or build rockets.

00:20:18.116 --> 00:20:20.786
They don't do a thing for
their people, the Hamas.

00:20:20.786 --> 00:20:23.322
You know, they execute.
That's what they do.

00:20:23.322 --> 00:20:24.623
They shoot them in
the back of the neck

00:20:24.623 --> 00:20:27.025
if they dare utter a dissent.

00:20:30.295 --> 00:20:32.731
They abuse their women,

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:35.200
they abuse gays and so on,

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.669
but that doesn't prevent
the international left

00:20:37.669 --> 00:20:40.839
from talking about human rights,

00:20:40.839 --> 00:20:42.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
talking about Israel
and human rights,

00:20:42.374 --> 00:20:45.077
and not about these thugs

00:20:45.077 --> 00:20:46.812 align:start size:97% position:3%
who do these horrible
things to their own people,

00:20:46.812 --> 00:20:49.848 align:start size:97% position:3%
just as until recently they
didn't talk about Iran,

00:20:49.848 --> 00:20:52.384 align:start size:97% position:3%
until those brave,
extraordinarily brave women

00:20:52.384 --> 00:20:55.187 align:start size:88% position:13%
went out in the street,
and this created

00:20:55.187 --> 00:20:58.123
a united front of left and right

00:20:58.123 --> 00:20:59.891
that finally sees
the true nature

00:20:59.891 --> 00:21:02.928
of this horrible
regime in Tehran.

00:21:02.928 --> 00:21:05.530 align:start size:88% position:13%
That hasn't yet happened
to the Palestinians,

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:06.865
but you can look,

00:21:06.865 --> 00:21:07.966
what do you think
is the difference

00:21:07.966 --> 00:21:10.168
between the Iranian regime

00:21:10.168 --> 00:21:12.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the Palestinian
regime in Gaza?

00:21:12.871 --> 00:21:15.407 align:start size:84% position:16%
The answer is nothing.
It's only smaller.

00:21:15.407 --> 00:21:17.576 align:start size:97% position:3%
And less well armed,
that's the only difference.

00:21:17.576 --> 00:21:22.147
But in terms of violating
the rights of Palestinians,

00:21:22.147 --> 00:21:24.716
and men and women
and everybody else,

00:21:24.716 --> 00:21:26.285
they're horrible,
horrible people.

00:21:26.285 --> 00:21:29.888
So you can't get peace,
if you talk about peace.

00:21:29.888 --> 00:21:32.524
The reason we haven't had
peace with the Palestinians

00:21:33.825 --> 00:21:36.561 align:start size:97% position:3%
is because the Palestinians
don't want peace.

00:21:36.561 --> 00:21:39.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, they've
been led by leaders

00:21:39.331 --> 00:21:41.633
who are committed to
Israel's destruction

00:21:41.633 --> 00:21:44.469 align:start size:97% position:3%
for now for a century, before
the existence of Israel

00:21:44.469 --> 00:21:46.438 align:start size:84% position:16%
and since the
existence of Israel.

00:21:46.438 --> 00:21:50.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they say they want
peace, but without Israel.

00:21:50.075 --> 00:21:51.810
They say they want a state,

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:53.845 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's not a state
next to Israel,

00:21:53.845 --> 00:21:55.681
it's a state instead of Israel.

00:21:55.681 --> 00:21:58.216 align:start size:84% position:16%
So one of the
things that happened

00:21:58.216 --> 00:22:01.520 align:start size:97% position:3%
as a result of what I just
described is that people said,

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:05.157 align:start size:97% position:3%
you have to first have
peace with the Palestinians

00:22:05.157 --> 00:22:07.693 align:start size:97% position:3%
before we can have peace
with the broader Arab world.

00:22:07.693 --> 00:22:10.495
Remember, the Palestinians are
one to 2% of the Arab world,

00:22:10.495 --> 00:22:12.564
both in land mass
and in population.

00:22:13.999 --> 00:22:17.202
But the regnant thinking,
the prevailing thinking

00:22:17.202 --> 00:22:20.305 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the foreign policy
elites (chuckles)

00:22:20.305 --> 00:22:23.275 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the foreign ministry
chancelleries of the world,

00:22:23.275 --> 00:22:25.577
you have to have peace
with the Palestinians

00:22:25.577 --> 00:22:27.212 align:start size:84% position:16%
or you won't have
peace between Israel

00:22:27.212 --> 00:22:29.114
and the rest of the Arab world.

00:22:29.114 --> 00:22:30.048
And I thought--

00:22:30.048 --> 00:22:31.283
- And you did it the other way.

00:22:31.283 --> 00:22:32.551
- Not only did I do
it the other way,

00:22:32.551 --> 00:22:35.654
we waited for 25 years,
a quarter of a century,

00:22:35.654 --> 00:22:37.489
that way we didn't get
anywhere, we couldn't,

00:22:37.489 --> 00:22:40.392 align:start position:0%
and we'd wait another half
century, maybe another century.

00:22:40.392 --> 00:22:41.993
I said, no, we're going around,

00:22:41.993 --> 00:22:43.195
we're going around that,

00:22:43.195 --> 00:22:45.197
and we'll go directly
to the Arab world.

00:22:45.197 --> 00:22:47.999
And as a result of the
rise of Israeli power,

00:22:47.999 --> 00:22:52.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of the revolution
that we led, I led

00:22:54.139 --> 00:22:56.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
to make Israel a
free market economy,

00:22:56.475 --> 00:22:58.577
which bolstered our
military and intel

00:22:58.577 --> 00:23:00.312
and cyber capability,

00:23:00.312 --> 00:23:03.548 align:start size:88% position:13%
we became very valuable
to other countries,

00:23:03.548 --> 00:23:05.217
valuable in civilian technology,

00:23:05.217 --> 00:23:07.953
which could better the
lives of their citizens,

00:23:07.953 --> 00:23:12.457
and valuable in terms of
offering security help,

00:23:12.457 --> 00:23:15.594 align:start size:88% position:13%
of fending off a common
threat like Iran.

00:23:15.594 --> 00:23:18.964
So what happened was, and
I could see this happening

00:23:20.065 --> 00:23:23.235
and I nurtured it to happen,

00:23:23.235 --> 00:23:28.240
is that Arab states began to
look at us not as an enemy,

00:23:29.107 --> 00:23:31.576
but as their indispensable ally

00:23:31.576 --> 00:23:34.246 align:start size:84% position:16%
in fending off
Iranian aggression,

00:23:34.246 --> 00:23:37.048
which would subjugate them too,

00:23:37.048 --> 00:23:39.451 align:start size:88% position:13%
and bringing a better
life for their citizens.

00:23:39.451 --> 00:23:44.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that view was, I
would say was dramatized,

00:23:45.857 --> 00:23:47.859 align:start size:97% position:3%
brought to a head in that
speech that I made in Congress

00:23:47.859 --> 00:23:52.330
challenging President
Obama's deal with Iran.

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:56.334
While I was giving that
speech, in real time,

00:23:56.334 --> 00:23:59.171
we got phone calls
from Gulf states

00:24:00.505 --> 00:24:02.874 align:start size:97% position:3%
in which the representatives
of these governments

00:24:02.874 --> 00:24:04.609
were saying, "We can't believe

00:24:04.609 --> 00:24:06.745 align:start size:81% position:19%
what your prime
minister is doing.

00:24:06.745 --> 00:24:09.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can't believe he's
standing up the way he is,

00:24:09.314 --> 00:24:10.816
because he's really
standing up for us.

00:24:10.816 --> 00:24:14.186 align:start size:84% position:16%
We don't have the
gumption to do that."

00:24:14.186 --> 00:24:16.288 align:start size:84% position:16%
But that led to
clandestine meetings.

00:24:16.288 --> 00:24:18.557
I'm talking about 2015.

00:24:18.557 --> 00:24:19.391
2015.

00:24:20.292 --> 00:24:22.160
That led to secret meetings

00:24:23.795 --> 00:24:25.430
with the Gulf leaders,

00:24:25.430 --> 00:24:27.766 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that laid the foundation
for the Abraham Accords

00:24:27.766 --> 00:24:29.568
that turned things upside down.

00:24:29.568 --> 00:24:32.270 align:start size:88% position:13%
If the idea was that you
make peace inside out

00:24:32.270 --> 00:24:34.840
from the Palestinians to
the broader Arab world,

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:38.977
I said, well, maybe so if the
Palestinians want to come,

00:24:38.977 --> 00:24:40.479 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we're not gonna
wait for them.

00:24:40.479 --> 00:24:42.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, we're gonna
make an inside outside in.

00:24:42.781 --> 00:24:45.016
We'll go to the Arab states,

00:24:45.016 --> 00:24:47.986
and finally, we'll double
back to the Palestinians.

00:24:50.489 --> 00:24:52.824 align:start size:84% position:16%
That produced four
historic peace accords

00:24:52.824 --> 00:24:55.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the help of President
Trump and his team.

00:24:55.694 --> 00:24:57.162
The Abraham Accords.

00:24:57.162 --> 00:25:00.999
Peace with the United Arab
Emirates, peace with Bahrain,

00:25:00.999 --> 00:25:03.101
peace with Morocco,
and peace with Sudan,

00:25:03.101 --> 00:25:05.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I've actually
come to this podcast,

00:25:05.871 --> 00:25:07.873
to this discussion of ours

00:25:09.274 --> 00:25:11.543
right from the celebrating

00:25:11.543 --> 00:25:14.779
the Independence Day of the
Emirates here in Tel Aviv.

00:25:15.881 --> 00:25:18.350 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you'd said two years ago--
- Yeah.

00:25:18.350 --> 00:25:19.618
- You know, (chuckles)

00:25:19.618 --> 00:25:20.552
if you said two years
ago this would happen,

00:25:20.552 --> 00:25:22.387
people would think you're crazy.

00:25:22.387 --> 00:25:24.422 align:start size:97% position:3%
I didn't think it was crazy,
I knew it would happen.

00:25:24.422 --> 00:25:27.225 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you told me that hundreds
of thousands of Israelis

00:25:27.225 --> 00:25:29.528 align:start size:88% position:13%
would be flying over the
skies of Saudi Arabia

00:25:30.862 --> 00:25:34.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
and dancing in the
streets with the Emiratis

00:25:34.266 --> 00:25:37.802
in Abu Dhabi and in Dubai,
you'd say, this is crazy,

00:25:37.802 --> 00:25:39.638 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it's not crazy,
it's happening.

00:25:39.638 --> 00:25:43.475 align:start size:97% position:3%
And this is the path to
peace that I intend to pursue

00:25:43.475 --> 00:25:45.443
with much greater,
even greater fervor.

00:25:45.443 --> 00:25:47.913 align:start size:88% position:13%
Not much greater fervor,
but greater fervor,

00:25:49.214 --> 00:25:51.616
and great opportunity
in the coming year.

00:25:53.018 --> 00:25:55.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
- How much of the (speaks
in foreign language),

00:25:55.153 --> 00:25:57.756 align:start size:88% position:13%
there's a word for you,
of the Middle East,

00:25:57.756 --> 00:26:01.326
is just people not really
understanding the history?

00:26:01.326 --> 00:26:03.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've heard you talk about
the history of Israel

00:26:03.562 --> 00:26:04.930
many, many times,

00:26:04.930 --> 00:26:06.298
but people not understanding

00:26:06.298 --> 00:26:08.333 align:start size:88% position:13%
that when you talk
about Judea and Samaria,

00:26:08.333 --> 00:26:10.335
which we now know
as the West Bank.

00:26:10.335 --> 00:26:12.637
Judea, Jews used to live there.

00:26:12.637 --> 00:26:14.973
Bethlehem, that's
where Jesus lived.

00:26:14.973 --> 00:26:17.642
That this is not a place
that Jews are foreign from,

00:26:17.642 --> 00:26:19.811
that people simply
don't understand

00:26:19.811 --> 00:26:22.581
the basic history of the land.

00:26:22.581 --> 00:26:25.016 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, you know,
in the modern world,

00:26:26.751 --> 00:26:29.721 align:start size:84% position:16%
you're lucky if your
historical memory

00:26:29.721 --> 00:26:31.323
goes back to breakfast.

00:26:31.323 --> 00:26:33.158 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's pretty good.
- Yeah.

00:26:33.158 --> 00:26:35.694 align:start size:81% position:19%
- But in our case,
I mean, people,

00:26:35.694 --> 00:26:37.529
you're right, they
don't know the facts.

00:26:37.529 --> 00:26:40.432
They think we're the
Belgians in the Congo,

00:26:40.432 --> 00:26:44.469
or the Dutch in Indonesia,
or some British colonials,

00:26:44.469 --> 00:26:48.106
I don't know, in some other
part of Africa and so on.

00:26:48.106 --> 00:26:50.175
And of course this
is not the case.

00:26:50.175 --> 00:26:52.110
As you say, Jews
came from Judea.

00:26:53.578 --> 00:26:57.115
King David. It's been our
homeland for 3,500 years.

00:26:57.115 --> 00:26:58.583
3,000 years ago,

00:26:58.583 --> 00:27:00.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
King David proclaimed
Jerusalem as our capital.

00:27:00.752 --> 00:27:03.054 align:start size:84% position:16%
The events described
in the Bible

00:27:03.054 --> 00:27:07.125 align:start size:97% position:3%
occurred for a period of about
2,000 years, actually less,

00:27:07.125 --> 00:27:11.262
but about 1,500 years
until the birth of,

00:27:11.262 --> 00:27:13.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
just before the birth
of Christianity.

00:27:13.264 --> 00:27:14.799
Now, where did that happen?

00:27:14.799 --> 00:27:19.270
Where did Jesus turn over the
tables of the money changers?

00:27:20.438 --> 00:27:22.974
It wasn't in a temple
in Tibet, you know.

00:27:24.142 --> 00:27:26.945
Didn't happen next to
Joburg in South Africa.

00:27:26.945 --> 00:27:29.914
It happened right
there in Jerusalem.

00:27:29.914 --> 00:27:32.684
And what language
did Jesus speak?

00:27:32.684 --> 00:27:34.653 align:start size:84% position:16%
He spoke Hebrew, and
he spoke Aramaic,

00:27:34.653 --> 00:27:36.454 align:start size:84% position:16%
he probably wrote
in Hebrew and so on.

00:27:36.454 --> 00:27:38.690
His name is a Hebrew name.

00:27:38.690 --> 00:27:40.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
He was a Jewish rabbi
from the Galilee.

00:27:40.592 --> 00:27:42.827
So there's an attempt to erase

00:27:42.827 --> 00:27:46.097
the first roughly 2,000
years of Jewish history.

00:27:46.097 --> 00:27:48.299
It didn't exist. The
Jews were not there.

00:27:48.299 --> 00:27:51.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, we were the original
natives of the land,

00:27:51.836 --> 00:27:54.039 align:start size:81% position:19%
and actually we
were dispossessed.

00:27:54.039 --> 00:27:55.240
You know, all these conquerors,

00:27:55.240 --> 00:27:56.408
people who conquered us,

00:27:56.408 --> 00:27:58.176 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Romans, and before
them the Greeks,

00:27:58.176 --> 00:28:00.378
and after them the
Byzantines and so on,

00:28:00.378 --> 00:28:02.514
none of them displaced us.

00:28:02.514 --> 00:28:06.017
Actually, the displacement of
the Jews from their homeland

00:28:06.017 --> 00:28:10.588
took place in greater numbers
and in significant numbers

00:28:10.588 --> 00:28:13.958
after the Arabs conquered the
land in the seventh century,

00:28:13.958 --> 00:28:16.895 align:start size:84% position:16%
okay, so it's not, the
Arabs were the ones

00:28:16.895 --> 00:28:20.031
who expropriated the
land from the Jews,

00:28:20.031 --> 00:28:22.300 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the Jews didn't
expropriate it from the Arabs.

00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:23.902
Well, that happens.

00:28:23.902 --> 00:28:26.771
So what, you're gonna go back

00:28:26.771 --> 00:28:29.674
now 1,300 years to
the seventh century,

00:28:29.674 --> 00:28:32.477 align:start size:97% position:3%
the Arabs came in, they
live there, it's their land.

00:28:32.477 --> 00:28:34.813
No, that's not what happened.

00:28:34.813 --> 00:28:38.083 align:start size:88% position:13%
The Arab conquest didn't
populate the land.

00:28:38.083 --> 00:28:40.185
They didn't build new
cities except one,

00:28:40.185 --> 00:28:42.787
communities, one,
one called Rama.

00:28:42.787 --> 00:28:44.422
Everything else was left barren.

00:28:44.422 --> 00:28:48.426 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they, too, were displaced
by other conquerors.

00:28:48.426 --> 00:28:51.496
Mongols, the Ottomans,
the British at the end.

00:28:51.496 --> 00:28:52.897
I won't get into that.

00:28:52.897 --> 00:28:56.468 align:start size:97% position:3%
But a succession of
empires governed this land.

00:28:56.468 --> 00:28:57.936
And it was nothing,

00:28:57.936 --> 00:28:59.404
it wasn't the homeland
of anyone except the Jews

00:28:59.404 --> 00:29:02.107
who never gave up the dream
of coming back to there,

00:29:02.107 --> 00:29:05.243 align:start size:84% position:16%
and over the centuries
Jews would pray,

00:29:05.243 --> 00:29:07.779
"Next year in Jerusalem,
next year in Jerusalem."

00:29:07.779 --> 00:29:09.781
It was only in the 19th century

00:29:09.781 --> 00:29:13.785 align:start size:88% position:13%
when a modern Moses
emerged for our people.

00:29:13.785 --> 00:29:15.286
His name was Theodore Herzl.

00:29:15.286 --> 00:29:18.223
He was 36 years old and he
worked only for eight years.

00:29:18.223 --> 00:29:19.724
That's it, for eight years.

00:29:20.658 --> 00:29:22.060
Giant of history.

00:29:22.060 --> 00:29:24.462
Because he died young at 44.

00:29:24.462 --> 00:29:28.466
And he said the only way
to have national salvation

00:29:28.466 --> 00:29:30.568
and to avoid what he foresaw

00:29:30.568 --> 00:29:32.403
would be the Holocaust in Europe

00:29:32.403 --> 00:29:34.239 align:start size:88% position:13%
would be for the Jewish
people to come back

00:29:34.239 --> 00:29:36.374
to their ancestral homeland.

00:29:36.374 --> 00:29:37.942
That return that began

00:29:37.942 --> 00:29:39.878
in the latter part
of the 19th century

00:29:41.813 --> 00:29:43.581
brought the land back to life.

00:29:43.581 --> 00:29:46.017 align:start size:88% position:13%
And as we were bringing
it back to life,

00:29:46.017 --> 00:29:49.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
there were people living
there, but very few.

00:29:49.888 --> 00:29:52.223
But there was a great
influx that came in

00:29:52.223 --> 00:29:54.359 align:start size:81% position:19%
as a result of
the Jewish return,

00:29:54.359 --> 00:29:57.829 align:start size:88% position:13%
influx of Arabs who came
in for better wages,

00:29:57.829 --> 00:30:01.499
for the factories,
for the hospitals,

00:30:01.499 --> 00:30:04.803 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the farms that
the Jews built.

00:30:04.803 --> 00:30:06.771
That attracted many Arabs.

00:30:06.771 --> 00:30:08.706 align:start size:88% position:13%
They now call
themselves Palestinians.

00:30:08.706 --> 00:30:11.476
They say, "We've been here
for thousands of years,"

00:30:11.476 --> 00:30:13.111 align:start size:81% position:19%
you know, from
the time of Jesus.

00:30:13.111 --> 00:30:14.312
No, they weren't.

00:30:14.312 --> 00:30:16.247
We had a verdant homeland

00:30:16.247 --> 00:30:18.216
when the Jews came here
in the 19th century.

00:30:18.216 --> 00:30:19.717
No you didn't.

00:30:19.717 --> 00:30:21.452
Mark Twain will attest to
that, and hundreds of--

00:30:21.452 --> 00:30:22.654
- (laughs) Yeah.

00:30:22.654 --> 00:30:24.055 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Nothing. You
had nothing there.

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:27.025 align:start size:97% position:3%
We came back to our ancestral
homeland, rebuilt it,

00:30:27.025 --> 00:30:29.727
accepted our Arab neighbors.

00:30:29.727 --> 00:30:31.729
But they refused to have
us, and they still refuse.

00:30:31.729 --> 00:30:35.667
So if you want to understand
the justice of the Jewish case,

00:30:35.667 --> 00:30:38.570
is we never gave up our
claim to our homeland.

00:30:38.570 --> 00:30:41.773
We are the native
owners of the land.

00:30:41.773 --> 00:30:44.976
We are the ones who have
every right to live there

00:30:44.976 --> 00:30:47.512
having been dispossessed from
it, first of all by Arabs,

00:30:47.512 --> 00:30:49.681 align:start position:0%
but we don't want to dispossess
the Arabs themselves.

00:30:49.681 --> 00:30:51.683 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're the ones
who refuse to do it.

00:30:51.683 --> 00:30:54.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you ask me, what
is the persistent obstacle

00:30:55.687 --> 00:30:58.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
to having an
Israeli-Palestinian peace

00:30:58.223 --> 00:31:02.193
as opposed to an Israeli-Arab
peace, which we're achieving,

00:31:02.193 --> 00:31:05.263
it's the persistent
Palestinian refusal

00:31:05.263 --> 00:31:09.300
to recognize a Jewish
state in any boundary.

00:31:09.300 --> 00:31:10.768
That's the problem.

00:31:10.768 --> 00:31:13.571 align:start size:97% position:3%
And because that's not gonna
be resolved right away,

00:31:13.571 --> 00:31:16.774
I say, go to the Arab world,

00:31:16.774 --> 00:31:20.678 align:start size:88% position:13%
get these extraordinary
agreements with
the Arab countries,

00:31:20.678 --> 00:31:22.347
and the greatest prize would be,

00:31:22.347 --> 00:31:25.884 align:start size:97% position:3%
without a doubt, Saudi Arabia,
which would effectively,

00:31:25.884 --> 00:31:27.919
peace with Saudi Arabia
would effectively end

00:31:27.919 --> 00:31:29.587
the Arab-Israeli conflict.

00:31:29.587 --> 00:31:30.889
And then do your damnedest

00:31:30.889 --> 00:31:34.959 align:start size:88% position:13%
to get the
rejectionist leadership

00:31:34.959 --> 00:31:38.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the Palestinian world,
Palestinian society

00:31:38.329 --> 00:31:41.132
to accept the right
of the Jewish people

00:31:41.132 --> 00:31:42.433
to have a state of their own,

00:31:42.433 --> 00:31:44.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
then I think we
can have a solution

00:31:44.903 --> 00:31:48.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the Israeli-Palestinian
conflict.

00:31:49.274 --> 00:31:51.442
But I think that's
gonna be the order.

00:31:51.442 --> 00:31:55.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
I had to change a perception
that had been ingrained

00:31:55.880 --> 00:32:00.084 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the minds of the experts
and the foreign mavens,

00:32:00.084 --> 00:32:04.188
and you name them, for
close to half a century.

00:32:04.188 --> 00:32:06.224 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'd simply challenged
it and I was--

00:32:06.224 --> 00:32:07.825
- The think tank people in DC

00:32:07.825 --> 00:32:09.394 align:start size:84% position:16%
probably were not that
thrilled with you.

00:32:09.394 --> 00:32:11.496 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, the think tank
people in Tel Aviv

00:32:11.496 --> 00:32:12.997
weren't thrilled with the idea.

00:32:12.997 --> 00:32:15.433 align:start size:84% position:16%
Basically, you
know, I have an idea

00:32:15.433 --> 00:32:17.602
that all think tanks
and many diplomats

00:32:17.602 --> 00:32:22.273
are all produced
in a secret plant,

00:32:22.273 --> 00:32:25.510 align:start size:81% position:19%
30 kilometers west
of Luxembourg,

00:32:25.510 --> 00:32:27.478
and then they're sort
of sent, dispatched

00:32:27.478 --> 00:32:30.181
to all the bureaucracies,

00:32:30.181 --> 00:32:31.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
the foreign policy
bureaucracies of the world,

00:32:31.549 --> 00:32:33.785
and they just chant this thing.

00:32:33.785 --> 00:32:36.187
The Palestinian conflict

00:32:37.055 --> 00:32:38.856
is the core of the conflict,

00:32:38.856 --> 00:32:40.825 align:start size:88% position:13%
always in the singular,
in the Middle East.

00:32:40.825 --> 00:32:42.327
No, it's not.

00:32:42.327 --> 00:32:43.695
The only way that
you can solve it

00:32:43.695 --> 00:32:45.229
is for Israel to become so weak

00:32:45.229 --> 00:32:46.564
that it couldn't defend itself.

00:32:46.564 --> 00:32:47.999
No, it's not.

00:32:47.999 --> 00:32:49.968 align:start position:0%
There's not gonna be peace
with the rest of the Arab world

00:32:49.968 --> 00:32:52.270 align:start size:97% position:3%
if you don't solve the
Palestinian-Israeli conflict.

00:32:52.270 --> 00:32:53.504
No, it's not.

00:32:53.504 --> 00:32:54.839
But you know, if
you invest yourself

00:32:54.839 --> 00:32:57.642
in this nonsense for decades,

00:32:57.642 --> 00:32:58.543
it's very hard to

00:33:02.447 --> 00:33:04.282
detach yourself from it.

00:33:04.282 --> 00:33:05.683
And so I--

00:33:05.683 --> 00:33:07.218
- I always find it interesting

00:33:07.218 --> 00:33:10.021
how it sort of mainstreams
itself in a bizarre sense.

00:33:10.021 --> 00:33:11.522
So for example,

00:33:11.522 --> 00:33:13.791
you know Rashida Tlaib, our
congresswoman in Michigan,

00:33:13.791 --> 00:33:15.860 align:start size:88% position:13%
who I have no doubt
you're not a big fan of,

00:33:15.860 --> 00:33:19.197 align:start position:0%
I think maybe she was even
banned from Israel at one point,

00:33:19.197 --> 00:33:22.800
every December she wishes
Jews a happy Hanukkah.

00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:24.035
But at the same time,

00:33:24.035 --> 00:33:25.236
she doesn't want Jews
living in the place

00:33:25.236 --> 00:33:27.205
that is the story of Hanukkah.

00:33:27.205 --> 00:33:28.473
Does she know about the hills,

00:33:28.473 --> 00:33:30.775 align:start size:88% position:13%
probably about two miles
from you right now?

00:33:31.709 --> 00:33:32.910
- Happy Hanukkah.

00:33:32.910 --> 00:33:36.714 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, Hanukkah
celebrated the victory

00:33:36.714 --> 00:33:38.383
of the brave Maccabees

00:33:38.383 --> 00:33:40.418 align:start size:84% position:16%
against one of the
conquerors of our land

00:33:41.853 --> 00:33:44.222
actually 2,200 years ago,
roughly 2,200 years ago.

00:33:44.222 --> 00:33:46.257
2,200 years ago.

00:33:46.257 --> 00:33:48.259
Jews were fighting
for their freedom

00:33:48.259 --> 00:33:53.231 align:start size:84% position:16%
against basically
the Seleucid Empire,

00:33:53.231 --> 00:33:54.599
which was based in Syria.

00:33:56.901 --> 00:34:00.505 align:start position:0%
It's named after one of the
generals of Alexander the Great,

00:34:01.873 --> 00:34:05.710 align:start size:97% position:3%
who actually had a positive
attitude towards Jews

00:34:05.710 --> 00:34:08.679
but his inheritors didn't,

00:34:08.679 --> 00:34:12.817 align:start size:97% position:3%
and one of them wanted to
wipe out the Jewish religion,

00:34:12.817 --> 00:34:14.886
and Jews rebelled.

00:34:14.886 --> 00:34:19.223
And this rebellion
led by brothers,

00:34:19.223 --> 00:34:21.692
who each died, they all
died in this battle,

00:34:21.692 --> 00:34:23.861
finally achieved the
liberation of the land

00:34:24.729 --> 00:34:26.898
and the liberation of Jerusalem.

00:34:26.898 --> 00:34:28.266
That's what we celebrate.

00:34:29.667 --> 00:34:32.904 align:start size:88% position:13%
Hanukkah is the
liberation of Jerusalem,

00:34:32.904 --> 00:34:36.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
specifically the cleansing
of the Jewish temple.

00:34:38.176 --> 00:34:42.246 align:start size:97% position:3%
So tell that to Rashida Tlaib,
I wanna hear a response.

00:34:42.246 --> 00:34:43.581
So were the Jews there or not?

00:34:43.581 --> 00:34:45.216
Were the Palestinians
there in Hanukkah,

00:34:45.216 --> 00:34:47.685
or the Jews were
there in Hanukkah?

00:34:47.685 --> 00:34:50.588 align:start size:88% position:13%
And this exemplifies
the tremendous ignorance

00:34:50.588 --> 00:34:52.890 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you discuss,
they just don't know.

00:34:52.890 --> 00:34:55.126
The Jews, the Jewish people,

00:34:55.126 --> 00:34:57.328
are probably one of the
oldest civilizations,

00:34:57.328 --> 00:34:59.464
or not probably, are
one of the two or three

00:34:59.464 --> 00:35:01.132
oldest civilizations in history.

00:35:01.132 --> 00:35:05.136 align:start position:0%
Our attachment to our ancestral
homeland is unmatched.

00:35:05.136 --> 00:35:07.638
A lot of people are attached
to their ancestral homeland,

00:35:07.638 --> 00:35:09.273
but they're not as old as us.

00:35:09.273 --> 00:35:11.843
And a lot of them lost
their ancestral homeland

00:35:11.843 --> 00:35:13.077
and disappeared.

00:35:13.077 --> 00:35:16.180
We're the only ones who
were kicked out of it,

00:35:17.582 --> 00:35:19.383
expelled from it, and said,
"We're gonna come back."

00:35:19.383 --> 00:35:21.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we came back, defying
the odds of history,

00:35:21.686 --> 00:35:23.221
achieved this miracle,

00:35:23.221 --> 00:35:27.892
built this extraordinarily
modern, successful state.

00:35:29.060 --> 00:35:32.497
We respect our roots, we
respect our neighbors,

00:35:32.497 --> 00:35:35.032
and we are bringing a
light unto the nations,

00:35:35.032 --> 00:35:37.802 align:start size:84% position:16%
principally by
incredible technology.

00:35:37.802 --> 00:35:40.138
And yet they say, you have no
right to live there, you know.

00:35:40.138 --> 00:35:42.473
We kicked you out once,
we'll kick you out again.

00:35:42.473 --> 00:35:44.142
No, you won't. It won't happen.

00:35:44.142 --> 00:35:47.879
Whether you are Hamas
or Hezbollah or Iran,

00:35:47.879 --> 00:35:48.813
it's not gonna happen.

00:35:48.813 --> 00:35:50.281
We're not gonna let it happen.

00:35:50.281 --> 00:35:52.316 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Well, it certainly ain't
gonna happen under your watch.

00:35:52.316 --> 00:35:54.018 align:start size:88% position:13%
I do wanna be
respectful of your time

00:35:54.018 --> 00:35:55.820
because it's late night
in Israel right now,

00:35:55.820 --> 00:35:57.722
and you are in the midst
of this coalition build

00:35:57.722 --> 00:35:59.423 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I'm sure you have
some things to do.

00:35:59.423 --> 00:36:01.225
I wanna ask you just
one thing personally,

00:36:01.225 --> 00:36:03.394
and I'll post the
link to the book

00:36:03.394 --> 00:36:04.795 align:start size:88% position:13%
and people can read
all about your history,

00:36:04.795 --> 00:36:06.297
and your brother,

00:36:06.297 --> 00:36:07.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's really some
remarkable stuff in there.

00:36:07.665 --> 00:36:10.034 align:start size:84% position:16%
But just on a
personal note to end,

00:36:10.034 --> 00:36:12.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've had to go into
the fire a million times,

00:36:12.570 --> 00:36:14.305
not only in the military,

00:36:14.305 --> 00:36:17.375
but in terms of going to the UN,

00:36:17.375 --> 00:36:20.978
giving these speeches, the
hostility towards Israel,

00:36:20.978 --> 00:36:22.647
standing up for your country,

00:36:22.647 --> 00:36:26.484 align:start size:97% position:3%
and your beliefs, and your
religion, all of those things.

00:36:26.484 --> 00:36:28.886
It can't be easy, it
can't be that fun.

00:36:28.886 --> 00:36:30.755
I mean, the amount
of hate and protests

00:36:30.755 --> 00:36:32.490
and all of this stuff.

00:36:32.490 --> 00:36:37.495 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I wonder, at your age,
coming back, doing this again,

00:36:38.696 --> 00:36:40.231
it's not the easiest
thing in the world,

00:36:40.231 --> 00:36:42.433
but you're doing it again and
you seem as energized as ever,

00:36:42.433 --> 00:36:44.802
and where does that
come from within you?

00:36:44.802 --> 00:36:46.504
And did you think
about not doing it?

00:36:46.504 --> 00:36:49.207 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, when the last
election didn't go your way

00:36:49.207 --> 00:36:51.108
did you think, "Okay,
let me just step away,"

00:36:51.108 --> 00:36:52.243
or you were basically fighting

00:36:52.243 --> 00:36:54.312
in the opposition immediately?

00:36:54.312 --> 00:36:55.646
- Well, there was one incident

00:36:55.646 --> 00:36:59.951
that I describe in
one of my defeats,

00:36:59.951 --> 00:37:01.352
because I've had a few defeats.

00:37:01.352 --> 00:37:03.621 align:start position:0%
I've had a succession of
victories, but also had defeats,

00:37:03.621 --> 00:37:05.756
and that question arose.

00:37:07.191 --> 00:37:12.063
I had one elections where my
party contracted to 12 seats.

00:37:13.497 --> 00:37:16.067
That's 10% of the Knesset.

00:37:17.268 --> 00:37:19.570
For comparison, we
now have 32 seats

00:37:19.570 --> 00:37:23.140
in a coalition of 64 out of 120,

00:37:23.140 --> 00:37:24.575
32 led by my party,

00:37:24.575 --> 00:37:27.478 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is by far the largest
party in the Knesset.

00:37:27.478 --> 00:37:30.348
A quarter of the seats,
more than a quarter.

00:37:31.215 --> 00:37:33.417
And a coalition that is solid.

00:37:33.417 --> 00:37:35.219
But here you get, this happened

00:37:35.219 --> 00:37:39.890
where I contracted to 12 seats,

00:37:39.890 --> 00:37:44.895 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I came back from
meeting the party faithful,

00:37:46.430 --> 00:37:51.168
there weren't too many in
that evening of defeat.

00:37:51.168 --> 00:37:53.104 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I said to my
wife, Sarah, I said,

00:37:53.104 --> 00:37:56.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Look, you know,
maybe this is the end.

00:37:57.742 --> 00:37:58.976
They eulogize me all the time.

00:37:58.976 --> 00:38:02.647
Maybe this time they're right.

00:38:02.647 --> 00:38:03.781
Why don't we just

00:38:06.550 --> 00:38:09.820
get on with our family,
with our two young boys,

00:38:09.820 --> 00:38:12.890
and with our life, and
get on with our life."

00:38:12.890 --> 00:38:17.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said to me,
"Bibi, this is your life.

00:38:18.829 --> 00:38:20.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
Don't leave it. This
is your purpose."

00:38:20.331 --> 00:38:22.600 align:start size:84% position:16%
And if you ask
what has guided me,

00:38:22.600 --> 00:38:25.603
what allows me to do this,
it's this sense of purpose.

00:38:25.603 --> 00:38:29.774 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's the fact that I'm
pursuing a mission,

00:38:29.774 --> 00:38:34.445 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the mission which I
inherited from my grandfather

00:38:34.445 --> 00:38:38.649 align:start size:97% position:3%
and my father and my
fallen brother is to assure

00:38:40.284 --> 00:38:42.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
the security and permanence
of the state of Israel,

00:38:42.653 --> 00:38:46.457 align:start size:84% position:16%
only by making it
strong and powerful.

00:38:47.792 --> 00:38:49.560
But I think it's not only

00:38:50.728 --> 00:38:54.265
my family and my wife and kids,

00:38:54.265 --> 00:38:57.368
two boys, who support me
and who share this mission,

00:38:57.368 --> 00:39:00.971
otherwise it would be
impossible to continue,

00:39:00.971 --> 00:39:03.741
but it's also millions
and millions of people.

00:39:03.741 --> 00:39:07.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
Not only millions
of people in Israel,

00:39:07.745 --> 00:39:09.680 align:start size:84% position:16%
millions of Jews
throughout the world,

00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:14.118
but millions of non-Jews who
see in the story of Israel

00:39:16.120 --> 00:39:18.255
a parable for humanity.

00:39:18.255 --> 00:39:20.191
Because if the Jewish people

00:39:20.191 --> 00:39:23.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
can overcome the most
dreadful odds in history,

00:39:23.361 --> 00:39:25.296
can come back from the dead,

00:39:25.296 --> 00:39:30.301
can ford this river between
annihilation and salvation

00:39:32.169 --> 00:39:34.638
and build this remarkable state,

00:39:34.638 --> 00:39:37.041 align:start size:84% position:16%
then there's hope
for all of humanity.

00:39:37.041 --> 00:39:39.910 align:start size:84% position:16%
And alongside the
defamation of Israel,

00:39:39.910 --> 00:39:43.280
the slander, the vilification,

00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:47.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to say there's
enormous, enormous respect

00:39:47.818 --> 00:39:50.621
and admiration and
sometimes adoration

00:39:50.621 --> 00:39:52.423
in many, many lands.

00:39:52.423 --> 00:39:54.592
And as Israel emerges

00:39:54.592 --> 00:39:59.163
as one of these rising
powers in the world,

00:39:59.163 --> 00:40:02.433
able to send aid missions,

00:40:02.433 --> 00:40:06.036 align:start size:97% position:3%
emergency missions to dozens
and dozens of countries,

00:40:06.036 --> 00:40:08.172
some of them hostile countries,

00:40:08.172 --> 00:40:12.309 align:start size:84% position:16%
to help people out
of earthquakes, or
hurricanes, or floods,

00:40:12.309 --> 00:40:16.180
and people see the true
nature of this state,

00:40:16.180 --> 00:40:20.785 align:start size:97% position:3%
and when they pick up their
cell phone and they understand

00:40:20.785 --> 00:40:24.522 align:start size:97% position:3%
that a good part of that
technology in that cell phone

00:40:24.522 --> 00:40:26.957
that makes their life
different completely

00:40:26.957 --> 00:40:28.192
comes from Israel,

00:40:28.192 --> 00:40:29.927
or when you navigate
in your car with Waze,

00:40:30.895 --> 00:40:32.163
another Israeli product,

00:40:32.163 --> 00:40:33.864
and it's endless,
it goes on and on.

00:40:33.864 --> 00:40:35.466
The medicine, the technology,

00:40:35.466 --> 00:40:38.836 align:start size:84% position:16%
the health, the
water desalinization,

00:40:38.836 --> 00:40:41.205
all these things that
are not pie in the sky,

00:40:41.205 --> 00:40:43.207
they're not, this is real.

00:40:43.207 --> 00:40:45.443
It's changing the life,
not only of Israelis,

00:40:45.443 --> 00:40:46.944
but of the world.

00:40:46.944 --> 00:40:50.614 align:start size:97% position:3%
Then there is also a different
admiration for Israel.

00:40:50.614 --> 00:40:53.484 align:start size:84% position:16%
The life of purpose
that I'm talking about

00:40:53.484 --> 00:40:57.388
says that the Jewish people
have come back from the dead,

00:40:57.388 --> 00:41:02.293
and we are here, and we
will continue to hold

00:41:03.627 --> 00:41:07.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
the high ground, literally
and figuratively.

00:41:07.398 --> 00:41:10.067
We are here and we're here
to stay. That's my purpose.

00:41:10.067 --> 00:41:12.269
And I would say to those people

00:41:12.269 --> 00:41:14.071
who wanna read my
book, my story,

00:41:14.071 --> 00:41:15.673
it's not really my story alone.

00:41:15.673 --> 00:41:20.678
It is my years in
an combat unit,

00:41:21.879 --> 00:41:24.048
I nearly died several
times in fire fights.

00:41:24.048 --> 00:41:26.350
I describe most of it

00:41:26.350 --> 00:41:27.184
within the limits

00:41:30.187 --> 00:41:32.323
of military propriety.

00:41:33.524 --> 00:41:36.160
And I nearly died
twice politically.

00:41:36.160 --> 00:41:37.661
But it's not merely my life,

00:41:37.661 --> 00:41:39.997
it's interwoven with the
life of the Jewish people

00:41:39.997 --> 00:41:42.032
and the Jewish state.

00:41:42.032 --> 00:41:45.236
But I think that there
is a larger issue here.

00:41:45.236 --> 00:41:49.540
I live, and I can say
this categorically,
a life of purpose.

00:41:52.977 --> 00:41:54.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
If you have a
purpose in your life,

00:41:56.213 --> 00:41:59.283
and preferably if it
goes beyond yourself,

00:41:59.283 --> 00:42:01.585
it will enrich your life
and make it meaningful.

00:42:01.585 --> 00:42:03.587
It's the only life worth living.

00:42:03.587 --> 00:42:08.225
And if you want to glean
some insights about that,

00:42:08.225 --> 00:42:11.061
then unabashedly, I tell you,

00:42:11.061 --> 00:42:12.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm plugging my
book, read my book.

00:42:12.796 --> 00:42:14.999
I think they'll benefit from it.

00:42:14.999 --> 00:42:17.935 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, we will link
down to your book below,

00:42:17.935 --> 00:42:19.403
Mr. Prime Minister.

00:42:19.403 --> 00:42:22.006 align:start size:88% position:13%
Cards on the table, it's
fairly obvious to me

00:42:22.006 --> 00:42:24.975 align:start size:84% position:16%
why the Israeli
people are giving you
another crack at this,

00:42:24.975 --> 00:42:26.610
and I suspect some
other peace deals

00:42:26.610 --> 00:42:28.212 align:start size:84% position:16%
and other good things
are gonna come.

00:42:28.212 --> 00:42:31.048
And I have to say that I
will be in Israel in May

00:42:31.048 --> 00:42:32.283
doing a few events,

00:42:32.283 --> 00:42:34.218
and you did break bread
with my good friends

00:42:34.218 --> 00:42:37.154
Jordan Peterson and Ben
Shapiro not too long ago,

00:42:37.154 --> 00:42:40.824
so maybe I can take you out for
hummus, something like that?

00:42:40.824 --> 00:42:41.892
- Got it. (chuckles)

00:42:41.892 --> 00:42:43.427
Let's do it.

00:42:43.427 --> 00:42:45.763
Maybe I can take you out. The
Israeli economy is doing well.

00:42:45.763 --> 00:42:48.732
- (laughs) It would
be an honor, sir.

00:42:48.732 --> 00:42:50.401
The book is "Bibi: My Story".

00:42:50.401 --> 00:42:51.702
The link is right down below.

00:42:51.702 --> 00:42:53.704
and I appreciate it,
Mr. Prime Minister.

00:42:53.704 --> 00:42:56.206
Now go do your coalition thing.

00:42:56.206 --> 00:42:57.374
- I'm doing exactly that.

00:42:57.374 --> 00:42:58.876
You think I'm joking,

00:42:58.876 --> 00:43:00.377
but that's exactly what I'm
doing in the other room.

00:43:00.377 --> 00:43:04.481
- (laughs) Thank you so much.
Really, truly an honor, sir.

00:43:04.481 --> 00:43:05.683
- Thank you.

